<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">23032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Pakistani jets struck a rehabilitation center in Kabul during Ramadan iftar, killing at least four hundred people — most of them addiction patients with nowhere else to go.</s> <s>The facility held up to eighteen hundred patients and was, for many families, the only treatment option in a country whose public healthcare system has effectively collapsed.</s> <s>Pakistan denies hitting a civilian target, but the Taliban's vowed retaliation as relatives dig through the rubble searching for the missing.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Sudanese military drone killed fifteen mourners at a funeral in Chad — not inside Sudan, but across an international border.</s> <s>The Rapid Support Forces have retaken the town of Bara in North Kordofan for the second time in ten days, using drones to overwhelm positions left without air defenses.</s> <s>Doctors Without Borders counted a hundred and twenty-three wounded civilians crossing into Chad by Monday, joining hundreds of thousands already trapped between two wars with nowhere safe on either side.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkey's barred all observers from the corruption trial of Istanbul's mayor, Ekrem Imamoglu, and four hundred and six co-defendants.</s> <s>Imamoglu broke the ruling party's twenty-five-year hold on Istanbul in twenty nineteen — the most significant opposition victory in modern Turkish politics.</s> <s>Human Rights Watch calls the mass trial a political dragnet; a conviction would strip the opposition's strongest presidential candidate from the next race.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers sexually assaulted a Palestinian herder in the Jordan Valley community of Humsa.</s> <s>Rights groups have documented a wave of similar attacks across the occupied territories this spring, targeting herding communities whose grazing land settlers are systematically moving to claim.</s> <s>The Israeli military governs the area and is legally responsible for protecting Palestinian residents — yet settler violence there faces near-total impunity.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Four Jewish ambulances were torched outside a synagogue in London's Golders Green before dawn.</s> <s>An Iran-linked group called Harakat Ashab al-Yamin claimed responsibility — the same network behind recent attacks on Jewish sites in Belgium and the Netherlands.</s> <s>Counterterrorism police are now working to confirm the group's operational ties to Tehran before declaring the attack state-sponsored.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Liberia has no law against female genital mutilation, and a vote this week could finally change that.</s> <s>The Women and Girls Protection Bill would create the country's first ban, but traditional leaders who perform the practice have mounted fierce political opposition in the legislature.</s> <s>Liberia remains among West Africa's last countries without legal protection — the UN's called for lawmakers to act before the parliamentary session closes.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's rupee hit a record ninety-three point nine-eight to the dollar as the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> crisis strangles the country's energy supply.</s> <s>The country imports eighty-five percent of its crude from the Middle East, and the disruption's already hit households — in Karnataka alone, cooking gas supply fell seventy-eight percent in a single week, with eighty percent of the state's hotels facing closure.</s> <s>Bank of America now forecasts the rupee at ninety-four by June, assuming weeks rather than months of conflict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba's signaled it'll discuss compensation for American property seized after the nineteen fifty-nine revolution — the first such opening in sixty-seven years.</s> <s>Six thousand Americans hold certified claims now worth nine billion dollars with interest, but Havana says it can't pay without trade revenue and has tied any settlement to Washington lifting its economic blockade.</s> <s>The offer puts the next move squarely on Washington, which has shown no interest in going first.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Gold fell ten percent last week — its worst drop since nineteen eighty-three.</s> <s>The Iran war's pushed oil above a hundred and ten dollars a barrel, flipping market expectations from rate cuts to rate hikes that punish non-yielding assets.</s> <s>Futures markets are now pricing in a Federal Reserve rate hike by October, and if that materializes, gold's twenty-five percent decline from January's record may only be the beginning.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Japan's Hayabusa Two probe has confirmed all five DNA nucleobases in pristine samples from asteroid Ryugu.</s> <s>Unlike meteorites contaminated on impact with Earth, these samples were sealed in space and returned intact — making this the first unambiguous proof that an asteroid carries life's chemical building blocks.</s> <s>NASA's OSIRIS-REx mission will analyze its own asteroid samples next, and researchers now expect to find the same signature, God willing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Of six thousand known exoplanets, astrophysicists have narrowed the list of potentially habitable worlds to just forty-five.</s> <s>Researchers ranked rocky planets by their potential for liquid water; top candidates include four worlds in the TRAPPIST-One system, forty light-years away, and Proxima Centauri b at just four.</s> <s>The James Webb Space Telescope now has a prioritized target queue, and the coming year's observations will determine how many of the forty-five survive closer scrutiny.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sixty percent of early-career grants terminated in the latest round of NIH cuts went to women researchers.</s> <s>Women are overrepresented in training grants — the category most aggressively targeted — and are less likely than men to hold multiple funding sources that could absorb the blow.</s> <s>The result is a structural setback for the next generation of women in American science, one that'll take years to reverse even if funding is restored.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>LG's new laptop displays deliver forty-eight percent longer battery life by dropping their refresh rate to a single cycle per second when screen content is static.</s> <s>Oxide semiconductors detect still images and throttle power consumption to match OLED efficiency — without the burn-in risk that's plagued organic screens for years.</s> <s>Dell's twenty twenty-six XPS line ships with the technology as standard; LG plans an OLED version by twenty twenty-seven.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nvidia's latest upscaling technology generates visual detail that game artists never drew — and gamers are calling it AI slop.</s> <s>DLSS Five uses deep learning to fabricate pixels between rendered frames, and CEO Jensen Huang insists it preserves artistic intent.</s> <s>No commercial game has shipped with the feature yet; whether AI-generated graphics become the industry's default or its cautionary tale depends on what players are willing to accept.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Solana now offers institutional clients four levels of transaction privacy built on zero-knowledge proofs.</s> <s>The cryptographic proofs let banks demonstrate regulatory compliance without revealing transaction amounts or counterparties, processed at speeds rivaling conventional payment networks.</s> <s>Regulators face a new question — whether auditor keys that can unlock data on demand satisfy anti-money-laundering requirements, or merely create the appearance of oversight.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>